From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:07:22 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] neocd-bios

The Neo Geo CD section gains a BIOS row, CDZ by default, then Front
Loader and Top Loader, kept in Config/neocd.txt (bios = cdz, front or
top). The CDZ loads fastest: on the maintainer's discs its longest
loading stall is 0.3 s on the host against 0.5 s for the other two.
The row is hidden while a game plays, because a model change resets the
console; it applies at the next insert, where NeoCD is told the value
it declares for that file, "neocd.bin (CDZ)", "front-sp1.bin (Front
Loader)" or "top-sp1.bin (Top Loader)". A state carries the BIOS ROM,
so a resume made under another model still loads.

Before a disc starts slot checks the chosen model's file in
BIOS/neocd/: present, 524288 bytes, and the crc32 of the libretro
database dat/System.dat row (neocd.bin df9de490, front-sp1.bin
cac62307, top-sp1.bin c36a47c0). Missing or the wrong size: the disc
stays on the shelf with "Neo Geo CD needs BIOS/neocd/<file>", because
NeoCD would otherwise boot its incomplete built-in BIOS without a word.
Another 512 KB file launches with one "<file> is not the known dump"
toast a session. A disc resumed at boot is checked the same way. The
six toasts upload after the Sega CD ones.
